  "createdAt" : 1737764544,
  "description" : "Directory of agencies licensed in Illinois as comprehensive or volunteer Hospice Programs under the Hospice Program Licensing Act (210 ILCS 60) and 77 Ill. Adm. Code 280. A Hospice Program is a public agency, private organization, or subdivision thereof primarily engaged in providing palliative care — physical, emotional, and spiritual support — to terminally ill patients and their families. Hospice services are delivered wherever the patient resides, including private homes, nursing homes, hospitals, and hospice residences. Each record represents one currently licensed program and includes the program name, location of the licensed parent office, primary administrative contact, license number, and license expiration date. Many hospice programs are also separately certified by the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) for federal hospice benefit reimbursement; CMS certification is independent of state licensure and is not reflected in this dataset. Licensure is administered by the Illinois Department of Public Health (IDPH), Division of Health Care Facilities and Programs, Hospice Program. Hospice Residences (separately licensed residential facilities operated by hospice programs) are published as a distinct dataset.",
